@@section 1
@@title SQ-TSY Trade sync, split-jar lang, Barbeque's Delight icons, 2026-11-03 ([trade_sync.md](../trade_sync.md), [barbeques_delight.md](../barbeques_delight.md) 4.6)
@@date 2026-11-03
@@jars creativecommon
@@sources feature_writeup/trade_sync.md feature_writeup/barbeques_delight.md
@@text
@@text Target: `creativeengineering-1.1.08.jar` (new `trader/TradeSync`), `creativedelight`, `creativebrewing`, `creativecalendar`,
@@text `creativecompat`, `creativeworldgen` 1.0.0, all built and installed in this instance's `mods/` 2026-11-03 (each Creative
@@text jar's lang moved from `assets/creativeengineering/lang/` to `assets/<modid>/lang/`). The trade rows need a **dedicated**
@@text scratch server and a client joined to it (singleplayer shares the tables and is skipped on purpose).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-TSY-01
@group A
@commands boot the dedicated scratch server; join with the scratch client; grep the server log
@pass `[trade sync] built N trade list(s), M listing(s) sampled` once (N = professions + 1), then `[trade sync] sent N trade list(s) to 1 player(s)`; no exception naming `TradeSync`; no hang at login (sampling skips map listings)
@fails a hang: a listing's `getOffer(null, ...)` locates; add its class to the skip test in `TradeSync.sample`
@reviewed 2026-11-20
bootexpect \[trade sync\] built \d+ trade list\(s\), \d+ listing\(s\) sampled
bootreject (?i)exception.*TradeSync|TradeSync.*exception
shell n=$(grep -ac '\[trade sync\] built' logs/latest.log); echo "built lines $n"; grep -aE '\[trade sync\]' logs/latest.log | cut -c1-200 | head -6; [ "$n" = 1 ]
look N in the built line = professions + 1; the `sent N trade list(s) to 1 player(s)` line and no login hang need the scratch client joined to this dedicated server (client half, run with the client session)
## SQ-TSY-02
@group A
@commands `/reload` with the client joined
@pass the `sent` line again, no second `built` line; client log shows `applied` again before JEI's reload lines
@fails `OnDatapackSyncEvent` player-list branch
@draft needs the scratch client joined to the dedicated server during the /reload (the pass reads the client log `applied` line before JEI's reload); qrun.py client drives an integrated server, so this waits for a dedicated-server client session
@@text
@@text Client:
@@text - CQ-TSY-01 (on the dedicated scratch server): client `latest.log` has `[trade sync] applied the server's villager and
@@text   wandering trader trades` **before** `[jei] Seasoning page`. JER villager pages: Butcher level 1 lists the six Barbeque's
@@text   Delight seasonings (64 cumin / pepper / chili powder, 16 of each sauce, 12 emeralds) and 64 salt; the Mechanical Engineer
@@text   and Chef pages show the pack trades; the Cleric shows only the pack's trades; the Wandering Trader page shows the pack
@@text   wandering list; vanilla rows (Farmer, Librarian books) still show. Pressing U on cumin powder opens the Butcher page.
@@text   Then leave and open a singleplayer world: same pages, no duplicates. Fails with `applied` after the JEI line: the
@@text   packet came too late; move the send earlier (login-phase packet).
@@text - CQ-LNG-01: JEI tabs Seasoning, Canning, Using Cans, Feast Plating show their titles; a Creative Brewing, Calendar, Compat
@@text   and Worldgen string shows text, not a key (pick one key from each `assets/<modid>/lang/en_us.json`).
@@text - CQ-BBQF-02: a skewer seasoned with each of cumin, pepper, chili and each sauce, and a skewer grilled on the Grill, show the
@@text   salt sparkle overlay; client log has no `Unable to load model: 'barbequesdelight:item/seasoned/`. WTHIT on a burnt
@@text   skewer on a Grill reads "Burnt".
